#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0106.1 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "THE SHEET'S OWN CASE, AND THE GROUPING DISCRIMINATOR (Fix #289 / M3-D6). DM declares NO STRAIN COLUMN AT ALL while TS and TX carry no STRAIN parameter either -- precisely the non-conformance the rule's own Description claims ('STRAIN is absent or empty in DM and no Strain trial-level parameter value is present'). Before M3-D6 this scenario was authored as expect=skipped: Requirements.Variables.All [STRAIN] rejected the dataset before the Check ran, and the machine guard var_exists(\"STRAIN\") would have suppressed it a second time. M3-D6 drops the scope entry and Fix #330 retires the machine guard, so the bare empty(STRAIN) leaf is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing, EC-43) and the rule now reports it. M3-D6 originally authored an explicit `not var_exists(...) or empty(...)` disjunct here; Plan B phase 4d' deleted the now-redundant presence half, leaving the verdict unchanged. TWO DM records: with STRAIN absent the first conjunct is true on every row, so a per-record rule would report twice; Grouping.Variables [STUDYID] collapses that to ONE finding anchored at the group's first flagged row. A report of 2 means the Grouping block is not being read."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SPECIES type=Char label="Species"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | RAT
S1 | DM | 002 | RAT
---

dataset TS class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | SPECIES | RAT
---

dataset TX class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Sets"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SETCD    type=Char label="Set Code"
col TXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TXPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Short Name"
col TXVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TX | G1 | 1 | TRTDOS | 100
---
